1
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:13,733
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,746 --> 00:00:45,960
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,106 --> 00:00:48,293
=Episode 19=

4
00:00:56,690 --> 00:00:58,770
He confined me without a second thought.

5
00:00:59,931 --> 00:01:02,130
Not even a word of comfort.

6
00:01:10,251 --> 00:01:12,731
I've been by your side all these years.

7
00:01:12,971 --> 00:01:14,091
Yet in your eyes,

8
00:01:15,731 --> 00:01:18,171
I matter less than Concubine Hui.

9
00:01:26,451 --> 00:01:27,011
Your Highness.

10
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:29,451
Concubine Hui found an excuse

11
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:31,290
to send Chunya out of the palace.

12
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:33,330
Concubine Hui...

13
00:01:35,451 --> 00:01:37,490
I underestimated you.

14
00:01:38,130 --> 00:01:40,930
If she'd sacrifice her own child,

15
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:43,811
what wouldn't she do?

16
00:01:44,531 --> 00:01:45,731
Your Highness, you mean...

17
00:01:46,251 --> 00:01:47,570
Concubine Hui's miscarriage?

18
00:01:48,050 --> 00:01:49,091
It's only a suspicion.

19
00:01:50,371 --> 00:01:52,210
That palace maid must know something.

20
00:01:54,410 --> 00:01:55,770
I don't care where she is.

21
00:01:56,731 --> 00:01:58,130
Find her!

22
00:01:58,731 --> 00:01:59,290
Yes.

23
00:01:59,531 --> 00:02:01,290
My uncle

24
00:02:02,531 --> 00:02:04,891
works at the
Construction Bureau, Ministry of Works.

25
00:02:05,451 --> 00:02:07,330
He's been vice director there for years.

26
00:02:07,971 --> 00:02:10,490
He has contacts in all sorts of circles.

27
00:02:10,731 --> 00:02:11,971
Have him

28
00:02:12,731 --> 00:02:13,811
handle this.

29
00:02:14,251 --> 00:02:14,890
Yes.

30
00:02:27,771 --> 00:02:29,170
Su Cao...

31
00:02:30,811 --> 00:02:33,450
You'd better hope I find nothing.

32
00:02:57,051 --> 00:02:58,010
Time for your medicine.

33
00:03:10,010 --> 00:03:11,491
I know you're still resentful.

34
00:03:12,331 --> 00:03:13,531
But Consort Chen has been punished.

35
00:03:13,931 --> 00:03:15,651
You should focus on recovering.

36
00:03:19,331 --> 00:03:20,491
I don't resent anyone.

37
00:03:21,971 --> 00:03:23,010
It's just that last night,

38
00:03:24,010 --> 00:03:25,651
I dreamed of a child.

39
00:03:27,811 --> 00:03:29,450
He stood far away.

40
00:03:30,450 --> 00:03:31,811
I tried to go to him,

41
00:03:32,570 --> 00:03:34,690
but I couldn't move.

42
00:03:35,450 --> 00:03:36,651
Then the child

43
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:39,811
called me "Mother"

44
00:03:41,410 --> 00:03:42,491
and walked away.

45
00:03:51,091 --> 00:03:52,331
Dreams often mean the opposite.

46
00:03:53,371 --> 00:03:54,730
We'll have another child.

47
00:03:55,850 --> 00:03:56,811
Don't be sad.

48
00:03:58,010 --> 00:03:58,931
Whatever you want,

49
00:03:59,570 --> 00:04:00,651
just ask.

50
00:04:01,651 --> 00:04:02,771
I'll grant it.

51
00:04:05,371 --> 00:04:06,531
Anything?

52
00:04:06,971 --> 00:04:08,170
An emperor's word is his bond.

53
00:04:11,010 --> 00:04:12,010
I'd like...

54
00:04:12,690 --> 00:04:15,531
to leave the palace every two weeks
to hold free clinics.

55
00:04:16,251 --> 00:04:17,491
In the imperial family's name,

56
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:20,371
I'd set up clinics in the capital

57
00:04:20,771 --> 00:04:23,331
to treat the poor and provide medicine.

58
00:04:24,331 --> 00:04:26,091
You haven't fully recovered.

59
00:04:27,571 --> 00:04:29,131
Why take on so much now?

60
00:04:31,091 --> 00:04:33,131
I just want to do some good

61
00:04:34,250 --> 00:04:35,610
for our next child,

62
00:04:36,290 --> 00:04:37,730
so they'll be blessed

63
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:39,410
and kept safe.

64
00:04:40,331 --> 00:04:42,451
I want our next child to arrive safely

65
00:04:42,610 --> 00:04:44,131
and grow up safe and well.

66
00:04:45,691 --> 00:04:46,410
Not like...

67
00:04:48,850 --> 00:04:50,370
not like the last one.

68
00:04:53,211 --> 00:04:54,651
I've lived among ordinary people.

69
00:04:55,531 --> 00:04:58,610
I know what matters to them.

70
00:04:59,410 --> 00:05:00,930
Heavy taxes aren't what they fear.

71
00:05:01,410 --> 00:05:03,531
They fear a court that forgets them.

72
00:05:04,331 --> 00:05:07,331
If I hold free clinics
in the imperial family's name,

73
00:05:08,211 --> 00:05:09,651
the people will remember

74
00:05:10,170 --> 00:05:11,651
Your Majesty's kindness.

75
00:05:12,971 --> 00:05:14,011
The people's support

76
00:05:14,490 --> 00:05:16,131
is the foundation of your rule.

77
00:05:26,250 --> 00:05:27,451
In this palace,

78
00:05:28,011 --> 00:05:28,891
you're the only one

79
00:05:30,410 --> 00:05:32,091
who thinks about these things for me.

80
00:05:38,170 --> 00:05:39,451
Che and I

81
00:05:39,930 --> 00:05:41,331
are one as husband and wife.

82
00:05:42,930 --> 00:05:44,250
It's only my duty.

83
00:05:52,610 --> 00:05:53,091
All right.

84
00:05:58,211 --> 00:05:58,971
Take this.

85
00:05:59,571 --> 00:06:01,610
With this, you may freely
enter and leave the palace

86
00:06:01,810 --> 00:06:02,850
and hold your free clinics.

87
00:06:05,250 --> 00:06:06,290
Thank you, Your Majesty.

88
00:06:09,531 --> 00:06:10,691
Once you've recovered,

89
00:06:11,451 --> 00:06:12,971
I want another child.

90
00:06:13,771 --> 00:06:14,930
One with you.

91
00:06:17,170 --> 00:06:17,610
Mm.

92
00:06:42,689 --> 00:06:46,876
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

93
00:06:47,010 --> 00:06:50,623
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

94
00:06:50,858 --> 00:06:53,457
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

95
00:06:53,494 --> 00:06:55,774
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

96
00:06:55,821 --> 00:06:59,650
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

97
00:07:00,052 --> 00:07:03,405
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

98
00:07:04,332 --> 00:07:07,845
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

99
00:07:08,345 --> 00:07:10,912
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

100
00:07:11,038 --> 00:07:13,071
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

101
00:07:13,138 --> 00:07:16,915
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

102
00:07:17,265 --> 00:07:21,598
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

103
00:07:21,821 --> 00:07:25,328
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

104
00:07:25,509 --> 00:07:28,362
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

105
00:07:28,429 --> 00:07:34,043
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

106
00:07:34,083 --> 00:07:37,097
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

107
00:07:37,138 --> 00:07:43,146
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

108
00:07:43,813 --> 00:07:50,800
♪The past has faded away♪

109
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:54,800
♪The past has faded away♪
